#1110 is fixed and committed as e40d9e1d. A -- on the command line now ends flag parsing: it's no longer reported as an unknown flag, and every word after it goes into the prompt exactly as typed. Build, the full cargo test, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass.

What changed, from running the built binary before and after:

| Command | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| yoyo -- hi | warning "Unknown flag '--'" | no warning, sends hi |
| yoyo -p -- --explain this | refused, exit 2 (-p took -- as its value) | sends --explain this |
| yoyo -p hi -- --x | two warnings; --x dropped | sends hi --x |
| yoyo --bogus -- hi | refused, exit 2 | unchanged |
| yoyo -- status | treated as a prompt | unchanged (sends status, doesn't run the subcommand) |
| yoyo --model -- hi | -- used as the model name | unchanged, and pinned by a test |
| yoyo -- --help | printed the help page | sends --help as the prompt |

No script or workflow in the repo calls yoyo ... -- ..., so nothing of ours depends on the old behaviour.

How it works:
• One rule, in `src/cli_config.rs`. A single function finds the first bare -- that isn't being used as a flag's value. Everything that reads flags now asks it where flags stop: the #1109 unknown-flag refusal, the old unknown-flag warning, the code that builds the prompt from loose words, the --help/--version early exit, and the main argument parser. Because the main parser stops at -- too, yoyo -- --model x no longer changes the model.
• One special case: -p -- followed by at least one word means "the prompt is what follows". Without it, the issue's own example (yoyo -p -- --explain this) couldn't work. -p -- with nothing after it behaves as before.
• Change outside the planned files: --help/--version are checked in src/dispatch_sub.rs, which wasn't on the task's file list. It's a two-line change, and without it yoyo -- --help would still show the help page and send nothing, which breaks the issue's done-when.

Tests:
• A table test in cli_config.rs covers no --, -- alone, dash-led words and a second -- after it, --model --, ---, --x and a bare -p --.
• The real-binary tests in tests/unknown_flag_refusal.rs now check that the words after -- appear in the request the test server receives.
• An existing test, flag_after_double_dash_keeps_the_old_warning, was asserting the buggy warning. I reversed it and renamed it to flag_after_double_dash_is_an_operand_not_a_warning rather than deleting it.
• Positive control: forcing the -- finder to find nothing turned the new table test and two of the binary tests red, by name. After restoring it everything was green, and no NEUTERED marker is left in the code.

Housekeeping:
• cli.rs went from 7877 to 7873 lines, and I updated its recorded size in tests/module_size.rs.
• dispatch_sub.rs is now 76 lines over its recorded size, but only 2 of those are mine. I left that as the non-fatal warning it already was rather than paste in the other 74 lines.
• docs/src/usage/single-prompt.md now explains how -- works.

Still open, filed as #1112 before the push closes #1110: a few flag checks run before the main parser and look at the whole command line. So yoyo -- --no-color hi sends --no-color hi as the prompt but also turns colour off. The --quiet/-q/--print check has the same problem. Separately, and older than this change, yoyo -p --help prints the help page instead of sending --help.

